WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.070 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  welcome to london a city steeped in  history and known for its iconic  landmarks  [Music]  british cuisine might not be world round  but  the city is full of great food that  extends way beyond its classic fish and  chips  first up an american classic with an  indian twist a londoner's favorite  [Music]  originally i came up with this idea when  i was only about 14 years old i used to  make them from my friends barbecues  culturally is a mishmash you can only  find this in london my name's alec i'm  from babaji's and we are in the  wonderful camden market sun's beating  down it's a wonderful day  the naga delhi double burger is made  with two fresh spiced lamb patties  served on a brioche naan style bun  between the two lamp patties is a crispy  onion bhaji on top of that we've got our  spiced naga deli double sauce it's made  with a naga chili pickle to give that  really authentic indian taste you'll get  sharp sweet spicy and then that lovely  juicy lamb on top  it's a big old burger you've got to be  hungry you have to try one mate  next up head to the windy streets of  soho and check out this small hole in  the wall serving up a traditional  chinese breakfast dish  i am proud to have brought an evolved  version of jam being to london  my name is seth  he and i am a co-founder of pleasant  ladies we are located in soho on greek  street pleasant ladies specialize in  jian bing some people call it a chinese  burrito like a savory chinese crepe  after we spread the batter on the hot  plate we then crack an egg on top spread  it out  flip it brush a house made sweet  fermented bean sauce chili oil a herb  salad after that it's your choice of  meat our house pickle and then your  chinese cracker and then rolled it up  and then you've got all your springiness  the chewiness the freshness and the  crispiness  i think that it's everybody's food  tucked away in a south london market is  a chip shop that isn't always playing by  the rules  i would say these are not traditional  chips but are a mix of different  cultures in one plate my name is marco  our shop is poptata and we are located  in tutti market in southwest london  one of our signature dishes is  definitely the guaca fries double cooked  fresh and cut chips  with the herbal seasoning a touch of  garlic  grill aluminum cheese from greece a  little bit of british cheddar mature  cheddar and there's mesh avocado fresh  both from the market so it's very  interesting because you got different  textures and different flavors obviously  the chips are crunchy and the cheese  with the heat of the fries of the chips  is melting on top  and then you've got the tanginess of the  sauce at the end so it's kind of windy  usually chips are served as a side but  what we try to do is for us to have the  chips as a main character so they're not  the side anymore  back towards the city center you'll find  a brazilian classic using an ingredient  we've never seen before  this is a traditional northeast  brazilian thing but it started with the  amazonia native tribes  my name is gustavo our shop is called  bay germany and is located at old  spitter fields market shoreditch london  this is beijou the closest thing would  be a flatbread in order to make it we  have to add a couple of spoons of  tapioca flour put on a hot pan once the  bottom is cooked you just put upside  down and it starts filling up to taste  inside the mushroom bijami there is  grated cheddar  mushroom with garlic and parsley  tomatoes red onions some chili goat  cheese  and spinach  it's slightly different than normal  bread because it is made purely of  starches so it's going to have a chewy  consistency  outside we leave it crispy our own way  it tastes incredible  [Music]  and finally for a twist on a traditional  aripa there's only one place we  recommend for this one  it's this spot  [Music]  in colombia we moda 33 type of arepa so  i found that mine has to be different i  have to get one step forward and that's  what i did my name is patricio mercado  my shop is mulatta and we are in  paddington in london the dish that i  created is called mulatta  mulata means is a mixed race  and the reason why i use my name is to  make me feel more proud where i come  from  to make the mulatta we open the kanban  we put guacamole chicken with the red  kidney beans a bit of cheese we put it  back in the griddle  melt the cheese and wrap it with the  cheese melted and we finished with the  torch of guacamole many people just put  the fresh cheese i use the cheese we  seal it and then it's a different thing  i just try to just recreate something  that will bring the roots of home so  it's something born here in london but  with the essence from colombian  traditions  you

